      "tier": "SUPER",
      "proposal": {
        "diagnosis": "Cyclic deadlock due to inconsistent lock acquisition order combined with a barrier held while locks are owned. Thread T1 locks A then waits at barrier; T2 locks B then waits at barrier. After barrier, each tries to acquire the other's lock, causing circular wait.",
        "root_cause": "Threads acquire locks in opposite order (T1: A\u2192B, T2: B\u2192A) and then wait at a barrier while still holding the first lock, preventing the other thread from progressing to release its lock.",
        "confidence": 0.95,
        "reasoning_summary": "The barrier wait occurs while each thread holds its first lock, blocking the other thread from acquiring its first lock and reaching the barrier. Moving the barrier before lock acquisition ensures all threads start together without holding resources.",
        "expected_effect": "Eliminates circular wait by ensuring no thread holds a lock when waiting at the barrier, allowing deterministic lock acquisition order after synchronization.",
        "risk_notes": [
          "Barrier must be reinitialized if reused; current usage is safe as it's used once.",
          "Print statements may reorder but do not affect correctness."
        ],
        "patch": "--- a/main.c\n+++ b/main.c\n@@ -10,9 +10,9 @@\n     int id = (int)(intptr_t)arg;\n     pthread_mutex_t *first = id == 1 ? &a : &b;\n     pthread_mutex_t *second = id == 1 ? &b : &a;\n+    pthread_barrier_wait(&ready);\n+    printf(\"T%d LOCK %s\\n\", id, first == &a ? \"A\" : \"B\");\n     pthread_mutex_lock(first);\n-    printf(\"T%d LOCK %s\\n\", id, first == &a ? \"A\" : \"B\");\n-    pthread_barrier_wait(&ready);\n     printf(\"T%d WAIT %s\\n\", id, second == &a ? \"A\" : \"B\");\n     pthread_mutex_lock(second);\n     pthread_mutex_unlock(second);\n"
      },
